## Vercel Speed Insights Configuration

Successfully configured Vercel Speed Insights for the Next.js project following the latest official documentation.

### Implementation Summary

**Modified:**
- `app/layout.tsx` - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component to the root layout

### Changes Made

1. **Fetched Latest Documentation**: Retrieved the most up-to-date installation instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart

2. **Verified Existing Package**: Confirmed that `@vercel/speed-insights` (v2.0.0) was already installed in package.json

3. **Configured SpeedInsights Component**: Added the `<SpeedInsights />` component to the root layout following Next.js-specific instructions:
   - The component was already imported but not being rendered
   - Added the component inside the `<body>` element alongside the existing `<Analytics />` component
   - This ensures Speed Insights tracking is active on all pages

4. **Verified Build**: Successfully built the project to ensure no errors were introduced

### Technical Details

Following the official Vercel documentation for Next.js (v13.5+):
- Import: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/next'`
- Placement: Inside the `<body>` element of the root layout
- Framework: Next.js 16.2.3 with App Router

### Testing

- ✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
- ✅ TypeScript compilation passed
- ✅ Project structure preserved
- ✅ No breaking changes introduced
- ⚠️ Linter warnings (pre-existing, unrelated to Speed Insights changes)

### Next Steps

Once deployed to Vercel:
1. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard for this project
2. Verify the tracking script appears in the page source
